  "description": "One line in the room chat. Player: what someone typed (in Draw & Guess a wrong guess is just this). System: neutral news, said quietly: joins, the game starting, a word revealed, a round’s mines. Score: somebody scored, said as quietly, with a check: a pair or trio found, a hand’s solves, a level cleared. Divider: a new turn or step begins, such as “Round 2 · Ana draws” or “Step 2 · Draw”. Success: a moment that matters: a correct Draw & Guess guess, the game won. Alert: something went wrong, such as a departure or a mistake. The viewer’s own lines are named “You”, as the Players panel tags them.",
